# Day 07

## C# / .NET concepts

- Task represents asynchronous work.
- Task<T> eventually returns T.
- async enables await.
- await does not automatically create a new thread.
- Avoid async void except event handlers.
- Async methods conventionally end with Async.
- Prefer async all the way.
- CancellationToken propagates cancellation.

## Architecture

Program -> Service -> Repository -> Storage

